# Angular Architecture

## Project Structure
**Core Module:** Singletons (auth, http, guards)
**Shared Module:** Reusable components, pipes, directives
**Feature Modules:** Business logic, lazy-loaded
**Standalone Components:** Preferred for new components
**Naming:** `name.component.ts`, `name.service.ts`, `name.model.ts`

## State Management
**Local State:** Angular Signals
**Component Communication:** Input/Output properties
**Global State:** Services with BehaviorSubject/ Ngrxjs
**Forms:** Reactive Forms with typed FormControls
**RxJS:** No nested `.subscribe()`. Use `async` pipe or `takeUntilDestroyed`

## Routing & Navigation
**Lazy Loading:** Feature modules loaded on demand
**Guards:** Route protection and data resolution
**Resolvers:** Pre-load data before route activation

## Integration
**API Consumption:** HTTP services calling `@dev/rules/stack/api.md` endpoints
**UI Components:** Following `@dev/rules/stack/ui.md` standards
**Data Flow:** Models from `@dev/rules/stack/data.md` DTOs